Now Playwright config/tests. Add gitignore entries.

Need think about screenshots full page with sticky headers and reduced motion. Fine.

`playwright.config.ts`:
- `testDir: "./tests/visual"`.
- `snapshotPathTemplate: "{testDir}/snapshots/{arg}{ext}"` to avoid platform suffix? Default includes platform. We want committed baseline; default is `snapshots/landing-wide-chromium-linux.png`. Fine. Use explicit template `{testDir}/snapshots/{arg}-{projectName}{ext}` with one project. Simpler default.
- `use: { baseURL, viewport, colorScheme:'dark', reducedMotion:'reduce', deviceScaleFactor:1 }`.
- `expect: { toHaveScreenshot: { maxDiffPixelRatio: 0.01, animations:'disabled' } }`.
- `webServer` command as above. Need ensure no old server on 4317.
- Add `workers: 1`.

Playwright test:
```ts
import { test, expect } from "@playwright/test";

test.describe("landing", () => {
 test("wide layout and CTAs", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.setViewportSize({width:1440,height:1000});
  await page.goto("/");
  await expect(page.getByRole("heading",{level:1})).toContainText("Turn unfinished ideas");
  await expect(page.getByRole("link",{name:/Try the example/}).first()).toHaveAttribute("href","/demo");
  await expect(page.getByRole("button",{name:/Connect OpenCode/}).first()).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.getByRole("link",{name:/Set up locally/}).first()).toHaveAttribute("href","#local-setup");
  await expect(page.locator("text=The example is a deterministic fixture")).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot("landing-wide.png",{fullPage:true});
 });
```
Snapshot full page maybe 8000px tall. Could be big. Let's see. The landing has many sections, likely 7000-9000 px. PNG maybe 1.5MB. Acceptable.
- narrow 390: `page.goto("/")`, check no overflow, screenshot.
- mode descriptions: assert text "A hosted instance can show..." and "never a visitor's local repository" etc. Also ensure no "trusted by" etc.
- keyboard: `page.keyboard.press("Tab")` -> activeElement class skip. Then tab -> brand. Check focus-visible outline width? `getComputedStyle(active).outlineWidth` maybe "3px" when focus-visible. Chromium applies :focus-visible for keyboard. Test.
- open dialog: click Connect OpenCode; expect dialog visible; press Escape; expect hidden.
- setup tabs: click Interface tab, expect command `npm run dev:web`; keyboard ArrowRight.
- contrast: evaluate token ratios. Implement JS in page.
- reduced motion: `expect(await page.locator(".spirit").first().evaluate(el => getComputedStyle(el).animationName)).toBe("none")`.
- workshop wide/narrow: goto `/workshop`, wait for heading; screenshot. Need ensure project loaded. `await expect(page.getByText("Plan outline")).toBeVisible()`. Then screenshot.
- check stage strip items count 4 and `aria-current="step"`.
- demo states: goto `/demo`, wait heading. screenshot spirit element cards. For each required: oracle listening, architect drawing, maker blocked, witness warning. Maybe also success. Requirement says "each spirit state" - visual snapshots for each state. We can screenshot all 16 state cards individually. That's 16 small PNGs ~10-20KB each. Good. Use loop:
```
const states = {...}
for (...) await expect(page.getByTestId(`spirit-state-${spirit}-${state}`)).toHaveScreenshot(`spirit-${spirit}-${state}.png`);
```
This covers every state.
- Run Inspector: `page.getByTestId("run-inspector").first()`. There is one on demo. Screenshot.
- errors: `page.getByTestId("demo-recovery")`.
- overflow/text zoom at 390 and 200% font. Check scrollWidth.
- mobile demo? maybe not.

Need ensure screenshot of element with `position: sticky` header not overlapping. `toHaveScreenshot` on locator scrolls into view.

Contrast helper:
```ts
const ratios = await page.evaluate(() => {
 const s = getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
 const parse = (v)=>v.match(/\d+(\.\d+)?/g).slice(0,3).map(Number);
 const lum = ...
 return {
  body: ratio(s.getPropertyValue('--text'), s.getPropertyValue('--ink-0')),
  muted: ratio(...),
  accent: ratio(s.getPropertyValue('--amber-ink'), s.getPropertyValue('--amber')),
  ...
 }
});
expect(Math.min(...)).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(4.5)
```
CSS custom props may have hex values, parse works (regex finds digits; for #f4f1e9 it finds "421..."? No, hex letters break). Need parse hex or rgb. Implement hex parser. Tokens are hex. Fine.

Focus order test:
- Tab 1 -> skip link. It is fixed at top -5rem but on focus top. Check `document.activeElement.textContent`.
- Tab 2 -> brand. Good.
- maybe the skip is first in DOM. yes.

Dialog test: native `showModal` inside effect triggered by React state; Playwright click. `dialog` visible. Press Escape triggers close event -> state false. Good.

Test setup tabs keyboard: focus first tab, press ArrowRight, expect second selected and command `npm run dev`; then ArrowRight command. Actually default initial is install. After ArrowRight, API. Then ArrowRight, Interface `npm run dev:web`. Test.

Workshop screenshot: engine unreachable; `loadEngine` fetch `/api/engine` returns 503 with JSON; `loadEngine` parses body available false. Good. `loadProject` returns project. Wait for h1 "What's still haunting". Then screenshot. At narrow, the stage strip overflow-x auto, no page overflow.

Potential console errors: Sentry tries ingest with fake DSN from env? `.env` doesn't exist maybe; VITE_SENTRY_DSN absent so no network. Good.

Server startup: `src/server/index.ts` imports `probeNativeEngine`, creates dirs in `/tmp/ub-visual-data`. Fine.

Let's add `.gitignore`.

