content.text:
Need update RunInspector to display model (optional) maybe not required for typecheck. But new operation/evidence types are compatible. Fine.

Need update `DemoPage`/teaser? They use demoOperations typed, now fixed. `RunInspector` type accepts. Good.

Need add CSS aliases for incoming styles and fix `.brand` override. Add at root aliases:
```
--bg: var(--ink-0);
--surface: var(--ink-2);
--raised: var(--ink-3);
--accent: var(--amber);
--success: var(--status-positive);
--danger: var(--status-danger);
--muted: var(--text-muted);
```
But incoming styles use `--space` tokens we have. `--bg` etc. Add. Then remove/adjust incoming `.brand` override to not break our brand. The appended `.brand` sets `color: var(--accent); font-family...; margin-right:auto;` It will make brand amber/serif; our brand name was serif and text color. Could be okay. `margin-right:auto` on brand within header flex (we already have actions margin-left auto; both fine). It sets no `gap` issue. But `.brand` in landing header gets margin-right auto, pushing nav? Our site nav has margin-left auto; with brand margin-right auto, both auto margins split, potentially nav centered and actions at end; could break. The later `.brand` rule applies globally. We should change the appended `.brand` block to only scope to `.workshop .brand`? Better delete it since our Brand component already styles. The incoming onboarding uses `<span className="brand">` in old App, but we're not using that. Remove the appended `.brand` block and `.settings-button` maybe not used. `settings-button` no longer used. Could leave.

Also incoming `a { color: var(--accent); }` appended globally will override our link colors (e.g., footer). It sets all anchors amber, maybe acceptable but our `.site-footer nav a` later? Incoming block is after our footer styles, so `a` wins by source order for color unless our selectors have higher specificity. `.site-footer nav a` specificity higher, so fine. `.brand` specificity class equal to incoming later; incoming wins. Remove.

Incoming onboarding styles use `.wizard-card .note` etc. Good.

Need add CSS for `.workshop-onboarding`, `.engine-dot.is-warn`, `.opencode` panel integration, and `.advanced` styling adapted. The incoming advanced styles use old tokens; aliases make them work. But `.advanced` width maybe full; within `.workshop` it spans; fine. `details` summary looks. We should add a top margin. Also the incoming `.onboarding` inside `.workshop` width full; good.

Need ensure `.brand` removal doesn't break `Onboarding`? It doesn't use brand. Fine.

Add aliases and remove block. Use edit.

